WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:04.776
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.843 --> 00:08.168
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.220 --> 00:11.647
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.698 --> 00:14.622
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.690 --> 00:18.218
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.303 --> 00:21.428
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.513 --> 00:23.032
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.100 --> 00:24.822
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.890 --> 00:29.823
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:39.118 --> 00:40.755
Stewie, what are
you doing?

00:40.823 --> 00:42.429
Oh, just doing a
little tai chi.

00:42.495 --> 00:44.920
You know how the Asians
look 30 until they're 60?

00:44.971 --> 00:46.157
This is why.

00:46.225 --> 00:47.812
Of course, then they
suddenly look 100,

00:47.896 --> 00:48.948
but cross that
bridge, you know?

00:49.016 --> 00:50.152
Is this a Japanese thing?

00:50.221 --> 00:51.574
No, Chinese.

00:51.641 --> 00:53.278
The Japanese have a whole
other thing going on.

00:53.842 --> 00:55.045
Hey, you want to see a movie?

00:55.070 --> 00:58.002
No, we're Japanese, let's watch
a schoolgirl bang an octopus.

00:58.148 --> 00:59.087
Yeah!

00:59.167 --> 01:01.289
(speaking Japanese)

01:01.355 --> 01:03.396
Suction cup feel good!

01:03.480 --> 01:06.857
(octopus and girl giggling)

01:06.908 --> 01:09.264
And of course the most
important part of any workout

01:09.332 --> 01:11.722
is a proper cool
down and a stretch.

01:11.790 --> 01:12.724
(screams)

01:12.793 --> 01:13.762
What? What is it?

01:13.830 --> 01:15.635
I got a splinter!

01:15.703 --> 01:17.541
(crying)

01:19.849 --> 01:21.670
Oh, my God, Stewie, what is it?!

01:21.738 --> 01:22.957
Oh, he's just
got a splinter.

01:23.042 --> 01:24.463
Oh, my poor baby.

01:24.529 --> 01:26.769
It's 'cause these old stairs
are just falling apart.

01:26.837 --> 01:28.074
It's not just the stairs.

01:28.143 --> 01:30.246
Meg has spent two days
pinned under a roof beam.

01:32.623 --> 01:34.661
Let's just focus
on the stairs, Brian.

01:37.838 --> 01:39.226
Morning, Opie.

01:39.294 --> 01:41.199
Hey, what's going on?
You going somewhere?

01:41.267 --> 01:42.871
(babbling)

01:42.939 --> 01:44.693
You got fired? Why?!

01:44.778 --> 01:46.515
(babbling)

01:46.583 --> 01:48.021
Oh, well, it's no wonder

01:48.088 --> 01:49.759
they finally caught you
doing that in here.

01:49.827 --> 01:51.197
I mean, the underside
of your desk

01:51.265 --> 01:52.903
looks like Carlsbad Caverns.

01:52.971 --> 01:54.308
(babbling)

01:55.830 --> 01:58.403
Griffin, say hello
to Opie's replacement, Stella.

01:58.487 --> 01:59.691
Nice to meet you.

01:59.758 --> 02:00.895
W-What is this?

02:00.961 --> 02:02.467
We doing a new
secret handshake now?

02:02.535 --> 02:04.540
No, Griffin, she's deaf.

02:04.607 --> 02:06.346
Oh. Can she
read lips?

02:06.414 --> 02:07.882
Yes, I can.

02:07.950 --> 02:10.959
So if I do this, I can talk
about what a sweet rack she has?

02:11.028 --> 02:13.583
Yes, but try not to make
a boob-honking gesture

02:13.652 --> 02:15.357
with your other hand
while you're saying it.

02:15.425 --> 02:16.929
Sorry.
It's okay.

02:17.013 --> 02:18.418
I'm used to people being

02:18.468 --> 02:21.226
a little uncomfortable
with me at first.

02:21.293 --> 02:24.086
If you have any questions,
feel free to ask.

02:24.152 --> 02:25.540
Yeah, actually, I do.

02:25.607 --> 02:28.750
Are your other senses better
on account of you can't hear?

02:28.818 --> 02:31.510
Like, can you smell my farts
before they even come out?

02:31.578 --> 02:33.448
'Cause I got one
in the pocket right now,

02:33.516 --> 02:36.257
and I want to know if I need
to feel self-conscious about it.

02:36.325 --> 02:38.130
I can't smell it, no.

02:38.197 --> 02:40.288
I might be able
to see it, though.

02:40.355 --> 02:44.049
A lot of people make small
movements when they fart.

02:44.134 --> 02:46.239
They twitch their
eye or something.

02:46.307 --> 02:48.245
Oh, like subtle
giveaways, huh?

02:48.313 --> 02:51.438
All right, well, t-tell me
if you can see when it happens.

02:51.506 --> 02:52.676
(farts)

02:52.744 --> 02:53.946
You just farted.

02:54.014 --> 02:55.250
Oh, my God,
you saw that?!

02:55.318 --> 02:57.993
You can see all my tiny,
subtle movements?

02:58.060 --> 02:59.146
(farts)

02:59.214 --> 03:00.651
You just did it again.

03:00.720 --> 03:02.290
Well, this is
gonna be a delight!

03:02.358 --> 03:03.945
I don't know
why Lois always said

03:04.013 --> 03:06.018
she had problems
with female coworkers.

03:06.087 --> 03:08.693
So Abby, Elaine and Janet have
their little lunch clique,

03:08.760 --> 03:09.964
and of course
I'm not invited.

03:10.031 --> 03:11.118
Seems like
you're doing everything

03:11.184 --> 03:12.455
and they're doing nothing.

03:12.523 --> 03:14.394
Well, I don't know,
but what I do know is

03:14.461 --> 03:15.715
that in the staff meeting,
- Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

03:15.783 --> 03:17.220
Christina said my inventory
system wasn't feasible.

03:17.288 --> 03:18.758
She's obviously
threatened by you.

03:18.826 --> 03:20.480
But when the associate sales
manager came back in the room...

03:20.549 --> 03:21.802
It's ridiculous,
and I support you fully.

03:21.869 --> 03:23.238
...she told him the idea
as if it was hers...

03:23.307 --> 03:24.343
You can't let them
get to you.

03:24.427 --> 03:25.814
They're jealous
of what you have.

03:25.882 --> 03:28.005
It's nothing to do with you,
and everything to do with them.

03:28.073 --> 03:29.878
Only you can
prevent forest fires.

03:33.390 --> 03:36.047
Hey, Peter, you ready
to go to the Clam?

03:36.132 --> 03:37.435
(quietly):
Whoa, who's the hot chick?

03:37.503 --> 03:38.690
Oh, that's Stella.

03:38.757 --> 03:39.993
You don't have to whisper;
she's deaf.

03:40.060 --> 03:41.013
Really?

03:41.080 --> 03:42.283
Oh, my God, that's hot.

03:42.351 --> 03:43.989
I didn't know you had
a thing for deaf chicks.

03:44.040 --> 03:45.309
Any kind of disabled
chick, Peter.

03:45.377 --> 03:46.648
They can do
things to you

03:46.716 --> 03:48.285
that regular chicks
don't even think of.

03:48.354 --> 03:49.657
Besides, you know me.

03:49.725 --> 03:51.145
I'm into a lot of
different stuff.

03:55.158 --> 03:56.579
What, did you hear something?

03:56.646 --> 03:57.647
No, it's all good.

03:57.715 --> 03:58.652
All right.

04:06.109 --> 04:08.533
You know, Chris,
a little friendly advice.

04:08.601 --> 04:10.205
Uh, you're gonna
start dating soon;

04:10.272 --> 04:11.878
probably good
to get in the habit

04:11.946 --> 04:13.398
of chewing
with your mouth closed.

04:13.467 --> 04:16.024
Doesn't bother me, I'm just--
you know, one friend to another.

04:16.092 --> 04:17.996
Oh, what, you got
a problem with me?

04:18.064 --> 04:20.505
You think I'm gross?

04:20.572 --> 04:23.379
Don't do that.
Don't do that.

04:25.672 --> 04:29.182
Yeah. This is what you are
and this is what I am.

04:29.267 --> 04:30.870
Peter, hurry up!

04:30.938 --> 04:31.975
You're missing dinner.

04:34.148 --> 04:36.021
(grunting, screaming)

04:36.089 --> 04:39.833
(bleeping)

04:39.884 --> 04:41.405
Lois, what the hell?!

04:41.472 --> 04:43.209
Oh, my God, Peter,
are you okay?!

04:43.262 --> 04:44.566
What the hell happened
to the stairs?!

04:44.634 --> 04:45.635
They're all
slippery now!

04:45.702 --> 04:47.339
I had them replaced,
remember?

04:47.407 --> 04:49.915
The old ones were so rough,
and Stewie got that splinter,

04:49.982 --> 04:52.556
so I thought replacing
the wood was the best way to go.

04:52.623 --> 04:54.062
When'd you do that?!

04:54.129 --> 04:56.402
The other day, when you spent
all that time at the drugstore.

04:56.470 --> 04:57.707
Oh, yeah.

04:57.775 --> 04:59.110
Couldn't figure out
if that Hispanic lady

04:59.178 --> 05:00.013
worked there or not.

05:03.759 --> 05:05.599
Um... excuse me.

05:07.973 --> 05:10.614
Excuse me.

05:10.682 --> 05:13.791
Boy, I wonder where the
shampoos are around here.

05:15.731 --> 05:19.476
I said, "I wonder where the
shampoos are around here."

05:21.715 --> 05:23.086
Oh, for God's sake,
I almost thought

05:23.155 --> 05:24.157
you were a
regular person.

05:24.224 --> 05:25.428
Where's the shampoo?!

05:25.495 --> 05:28.404
(rock music playing inside)

05:28.489 --> 05:30.576
What the hell?

05:30.645 --> 05:33.352
(people chattering)

05:35.678 --> 05:37.716
Hey, guys,
all the action's over here!

05:37.767 --> 05:40.208
Quagmire, what
is all this?

05:40.276 --> 05:42.163
Peter's new coworker
gave me an idea.

05:42.232 --> 05:44.688
Welcome to
Disabled Ladies Night.

05:44.757 --> 05:46.193
Mine are made
from teak.

05:46.260 --> 05:47.598
What are yours
made from?

05:47.666 --> 05:50.474
Yeah, mine are actually just
pressboard with wood veneer.

05:50.540 --> 05:52.012
I can't get wet.

05:52.080 --> 05:54.905
Oh. I think I
see my friends.

05:57.798 --> 05:59.954
Hey, uh, you guys
enjoy the carnival.

06:00.005 --> 06:02.795
I'm gonna get
a drink at the bar.

06:02.847 --> 06:04.769
Hey, uh, anyone
sitting here?

06:04.838 --> 06:05.956
No, go ahead.

06:06.024 --> 06:07.361
Thanks.

06:07.428 --> 06:09.334
Hey, would you like
to go out sometime?

06:09.401 --> 06:10.805
Wow, that was fast.

06:10.872 --> 06:12.996
Yeah, well, you know, I read
somewhere that women decide

06:13.064 --> 06:15.219
within the first seven seconds
if they're interested in you

06:15.287 --> 06:17.292
or not, so I figured I
wouldn't waste anybody's time.

06:17.360 --> 06:18.295
Fair enough.

06:18.363 --> 06:19.682
Sure, let's go out.

06:19.750 --> 06:20.753
- Really?
- Yeah.

06:20.822 --> 06:22.658
Like you said,
I've already decided.

06:22.727 --> 06:23.663
I'm Kate.

06:23.731 --> 06:24.934
I'm Brian.

06:25.002 --> 06:26.907
Hey, uh, you want
to go outside?

06:26.973 --> 06:27.942
Maybe a little
quieter.

06:28.010 --> 06:29.365
Sure.

06:33.746 --> 06:35.500
Oh, my God, I...

06:35.569 --> 06:37.221
Hey, check out Brian
with the blind chick.

06:37.290 --> 06:38.560
Hey, don't worry, Brian,

06:38.628 --> 06:39.998
you're still doing
better than Quagmire.

06:40.065 --> 06:41.167
He got a hooker.

06:41.236 --> 06:43.040
Ha!

06:43.109 --> 06:44.511
No, no, but she is
a prostitute.

06:52.864 --> 06:55.454
Listen, you know, we can do
something else if you want.

06:55.522 --> 06:56.892
Why? I'm having a good time.

06:56.960 --> 06:58.413
Well, I mean, I
just don't know

06:58.482 --> 07:01.323
how much fun it is for a blind
person to go to the movies.

07:01.391 --> 07:03.899
Brian, blind people
go to the movies all the time.

07:03.965 --> 07:05.301
We just listen.

07:05.370 --> 07:07.944
I might be blind, but my brain
has been trained to listen

07:08.012 --> 07:11.288
to any movie and know exactly
what's happening on screen.

07:11.356 --> 07:13.328
<i>Like, I loved Titanic.</i>

07:13.395 --> 07:15.820
I'm the king of the world!

07:15.903 --> 07:17.540
(orchestral music playing)

07:17.609 --> 07:20.835
(whooping)

07:24.532 --> 07:27.038
So you sure you don't
need me to come in?

07:27.106 --> 07:29.160
Maybe show you
to your bed.

07:29.245 --> 07:31.367
Pretty sure I can
find it, thanks.

07:31.436 --> 07:33.041
Maybe next time I'll
have trouble, though.

07:33.108 --> 07:35.213
You might have to help
me find it next time.

07:35.281 --> 07:36.718
So there's a next time.

07:36.787 --> 07:37.705
Definitely.

07:37.773 --> 07:38.675
Great.

07:38.743 --> 07:41.182
Well, all right, good night.

07:41.250 --> 07:42.520
(dog barking)

07:42.588 --> 07:45.263
Ugh! Our stupid
neighbor's dog barks 24/7.

07:45.331 --> 07:46.933
God, I hate dogs.

07:47.001 --> 07:48.457
Y-You do?

07:48.523 --> 07:52.300
Yeah, they're just slobbery,
annoying, needy little bastards.

07:52.368 --> 07:54.408
I'm just not really a
dog person, I guess.

07:54.476 --> 07:56.816
Oh. Uh, yeah, me neither.

07:56.884 --> 07:58.637
Dog people can get
pretty annoying.

07:58.706 --> 08:00.660
Wow, this is
a nice apartment you have.

08:00.728 --> 08:02.032
Is this your dog?

08:02.100 --> 08:05.276
Yes. Isn't he the cutest
little cutie wutie?

08:05.345 --> 08:06.780
Look how cute he is.

08:06.847 --> 08:08.152
Yes, he's very cute.

08:08.219 --> 08:09.589
Yes, he's cute.

08:09.657 --> 08:11.646
Yes, he's cute,
cute, cute, cute.

08:11.713 --> 08:13.537
Look at him. Look
at him. Look at him.

08:13.603 --> 08:14.672
(chuckles):
Okay.

08:14.741 --> 08:16.913
Look at it! Look at
that face! Come on!

08:16.980 --> 08:18.734
Look at that face!
You look at him!

08:18.803 --> 08:20.306
Look at that
(bleep) face!

08:22.448 --> 08:24.822
PETER: Hey, guys, this is
driving me nuts.

08:24.873 --> 08:26.711
Was one of the dwarves
named Snappy?

08:26.795 --> 08:27.882
Kind of well dressed?

08:27.966 --> 08:29.536
Or am I-I just making that up?

08:29.603 --> 08:31.042
(grunting, screaming)

08:31.110 --> 08:34.553
(bleeping)

08:34.620 --> 08:35.939
Oh, my God, Dad!

08:36.007 --> 08:37.311
Dad, are you okay?!

08:37.379 --> 08:38.983
Damn it, I hate
these new stairs!

08:39.050 --> 08:40.254
Yeah, I'm fine.

08:40.321 --> 08:41.457
I'll just--
I'm-I'm just gonna

08:41.525 --> 08:43.397
lie here until the
pain goes away.

08:43.465 --> 08:45.101
What are you
guys watching?

08:45.170 --> 08:47.075
ANNOUNCER: We now return to
the first time travel movie

08:47.143 --> 08:48.981
with a perfectly functioning
time machine.

08:49.049 --> 08:50.685
All right, if I'm correct,

08:50.753 --> 08:53.295
this should land us
in six million B.C.

08:55.520 --> 08:56.890
Quick!
Get us out of here!

08:59.013 --> 09:00.418
Boy, that was close.

09:00.485 --> 09:01.789
Oh, my God,
where's Frank?!

09:01.856 --> 09:03.093
I'm over here.

09:03.161 --> 09:04.331
Oh, okay.

09:10.901 --> 09:13.175
Brian, if I ever
take up roller derby,

09:13.242 --> 09:14.846
what do you think
my name should be?

09:14.914 --> 09:18.023
Bruisin' B. Anthony,
Alicia Sleaze or Quahag?

09:18.092 --> 09:19.828
How about Harlot O'Scara?

09:19.897 --> 09:21.117
Aw, you dick,
that's genius.

09:21.184 --> 09:22.353
How'd your date go?

09:22.421 --> 09:24.259
Aw, went great.
We had an awesome time.

09:24.327 --> 09:25.966
She's really smart,
really funny.

09:26.034 --> 09:27.236
Cute?
Yeah, hot, actually.

09:27.303 --> 09:28.707
I don't know
how she does it,

09:28.776 --> 09:30.647
but she dresses really well
for a blind girl.

09:30.715 --> 09:32.218
I mean, like,
her body is just...

09:32.286 --> 09:34.994
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

09:35.063 --> 09:35.997
What?

09:36.065 --> 09:37.099
Don't "what" me.

09:37.168 --> 09:38.337
You just said
she's blind.

09:38.405 --> 09:39.542
You just said it.

09:39.608 --> 09:40.945
You totally
buried the lead.

09:41.014 --> 09:42.417
Yeah, well, it's not
that important.

09:42.485 --> 09:43.923
So what if she can't see?

09:43.989 --> 09:45.627
She's amazing
in every other way.

09:45.696 --> 09:47.333
Okay, if you say so.

09:47.401 --> 09:49.775
Hey, does she have really
weird, messed-up eyes?

09:49.843 --> 09:51.278
No, her eyes are normal.

09:51.347 --> 09:53.669
They're beautiful, actually.

09:53.737 --> 09:55.543
Bet they're not.

09:55.610 --> 09:58.236
Bet they look like bowls of milk.
Shut up.

09:58.303 --> 09:59.705
You sure she isn't
just using you?

09:59.773 --> 10:01.009
Seeing-eye dogs are expensive;

10:01.078 --> 10:03.284
she may just be trying
to get one for free.

10:03.353 --> 10:05.322
No, actually, she doesn't
want a seeing-eye dog.

10:05.390 --> 10:07.597
She hates dogs.

10:07.666 --> 10:08.700
What?

10:08.768 --> 10:09.838
She doesn't like dogs.

10:09.906 --> 10:11.376
She's just not a dog person.

10:11.444 --> 10:13.148
What? Does she not
know you're a dog?

10:13.216 --> 10:14.418
How is that possible?

10:14.486 --> 10:17.061
Well, we-we haven't
done anything yet.

10:17.129 --> 10:19.468
So I'm-I'm just gonna, I'm just
gonna avoid touching her

10:19.536 --> 10:21.006
until a little more time
has passed.

10:21.074 --> 10:23.649
And by the time I tell her,
I'll have impressed her so much

10:23.717 --> 10:25.103
that the dog thing
won't even matter.

10:25.171 --> 10:26.423
Yeah, well, good
luck with that.

10:26.491 --> 10:28.464
You know, I like
your delusion, Brian.

10:28.531 --> 10:31.104
Most people would say,
"I lost, I give up,"

10:31.173 --> 10:33.011
but you, you just
keep trying.

10:33.080 --> 10:34.883
You're like the
Dominican Republic.

10:34.951 --> 10:36.957
Always killing the guy
in charge and saying,

10:37.025 --> 10:39.933
"Oh, this new guy, this new
guy's gonna get it right."

10:40.002 --> 10:41.539
Well, that's just because
I have confidence

10:41.607 --> 10:42.876
that I'll find happiness.

10:42.943 --> 10:44.382
Hey, anything's
possible, right?

10:44.449 --> 10:46.053
I mean, I once
found the Batcave.

10:46.120 --> 10:48.461
Look, you can't expect
to hire 60 workers

10:48.529 --> 10:51.469
to dig a cave under your house
and then keep it a secret.

10:51.537 --> 10:53.343
I mean, those men
live in this town.

10:53.411 --> 10:55.952
Yeah, but I told them it was
part of a geological survey.

10:56.019 --> 10:57.438
Batman, Batman.

10:57.489 --> 11:01.001
They built a lazy Susan
for your nuclear car.

11:01.069 --> 11:03.859
That's something they consider
conversation-worthy.

11:07.103 --> 11:09.611
Gosh, this has been
an amazing week, Brian.

11:09.679 --> 11:11.215
I still can't believe
you beat up

11:11.283 --> 11:12.653
that guy
who tried to mug us.

11:12.704 --> 11:14.075
That was a great dinner.

11:14.161 --> 11:16.032
Yeah, I really liked that
salmon you recommended.

11:16.083 --> 11:17.770
Yes. May I help
you gentlemen?

11:17.838 --> 11:19.392
(disguised voice): "Hey, you're in a
tough part of town.

11:19.477 --> 11:20.979
Now, give me your
purse, doll face."

11:21.048 --> 11:22.336
Hey, you get your
hands off that!

11:22.404 --> 11:23.772
I don't care how many
of you there are--

11:23.839 --> 11:25.144
you're not taking
this purse!

11:25.211 --> 11:26.915
"Ah, the hell we aren't.
Let's get him, boys!"

11:26.983 --> 11:28.537
Brian?
Stay right there, Kate.

11:28.606 --> 11:29.707
I'll handle this.

11:29.775 --> 11:31.130
(grunting)

11:31.198 --> 11:32.851
Yeah, you like
that, huh?

11:32.918 --> 11:33.971
"Ooh! This
guy's tough!"

11:34.056 --> 11:35.309
(grunting)

11:35.377 --> 11:36.815
"No fair. He
knows karate.

11:36.882 --> 11:39.122
Usually, handsome guys ain't
so good with their fists."

11:39.190 --> 11:40.675
(grunting)

11:40.743 --> 11:42.298
And stay away from
my girlfriend.

11:42.383 --> 11:43.585
Brian, I know
karate, too.

11:43.654 --> 11:44.840
I can help you.

11:44.925 --> 11:46.244
"You stay out
of this, lady!"

11:46.311 --> 11:47.900
(groaning)

11:47.967 --> 11:50.172
I got one!
I think I got one!

11:50.240 --> 11:52.313
Yeah, yeah, but I-I
got the other four.

11:52.381 --> 11:53.819
They're-they're
gone now.

11:53.885 --> 11:55.055
They're gone.

11:55.122 --> 11:56.994
Well, they took the
gift I had for you,

11:57.062 --> 11:58.165
but at least
you're okay.

11:58.232 --> 11:59.904
And that trip
to the Eiffel Tower

11:59.973 --> 12:01.374
was just amazing.

12:03.348 --> 12:04.618
(panting)

12:04.687 --> 12:06.424
Are we almost
at the top?

12:06.492 --> 12:08.248
Yeah, just a
few more steps.

12:08.315 --> 12:10.169
Here we are.

12:10.220 --> 12:12.427
Ah, the winds of Paris.

12:12.513 --> 12:14.099
Isn't that what they say?

12:14.167 --> 12:16.222
Oh, that breeze
is gorgeous.

12:16.291 --> 12:18.663
And I think I smell...
croissants?

12:18.730 --> 12:19.951
Do you?

12:20.036 --> 12:21.840
You have an amazing
sense of smell.

12:21.909 --> 12:23.044
Oh, there it is.

12:23.112 --> 12:24.381
There's what?
Oh, nothing.

12:24.433 --> 12:25.804
Just the, uh,
Goodyear blimp.

12:25.887 --> 12:28.278
It says, "I love you,
Kate," all in lights.

12:28.361 --> 12:30.033
(gasps)
Here in Paris?

12:30.101 --> 12:32.390
Yeah, it's... it's here for
Wimbledon or something.

12:32.458 --> 12:33.744
Oh, my God.

12:33.795 --> 12:34.882
That's the most
romantic thing

12:34.949 --> 12:36.285
anybody's ever
done for me.

12:36.337 --> 12:37.592
Well, get used to it.

12:37.643 --> 12:39.178
You're going to be
hearing a lot of things

12:39.263 --> 12:40.416
I've done for you.

12:43.811 --> 12:45.549
<i>ANNOUNCER:
We now return to True Blood.</i>

12:45.617 --> 12:47.488
Hi. I'm a nude vampire.

12:47.556 --> 12:49.795
Hi. I'm a nude werewolf.

12:49.864 --> 12:51.266
And that's the show!

12:51.334 --> 12:52.838
Peter, come downstairs.

12:52.905 --> 12:54.511
That gay show you like is on.

12:54.580 --> 12:55.648
PETER:
Coming!

13:11.231 --> 13:13.637
(screaming)

13:13.706 --> 13:16.145
(repeated bleeping)

13:16.214 --> 13:17.516
Damn it!

13:17.585 --> 13:19.172
Oh, my God, Peter.
Are you okay?

13:19.240 --> 13:20.878
No, I am not okay!

13:20.946 --> 13:22.784
Nothing about this
is okay!

13:22.851 --> 13:24.456
You just need
to be more careful

13:24.524 --> 13:25.994
coming down the stairs.
That's all.

13:26.060 --> 13:27.950
(grunts)
Easy for you to say.

13:28.017 --> 13:30.107
This is stressing
the crap out of me.

13:30.175 --> 13:32.715
Like when we had that
easily startled wallpaper.

13:34.320 --> 13:36.093
(voices screaming)
Aah!

13:43.500 --> 13:44.637
Well, it's getting late.

13:44.704 --> 13:46.024
I should probably go.

13:46.109 --> 13:48.382
Brian, this is like
our sixth date.

13:48.449 --> 13:49.953
I'm beginning to feel
like you're not

13:50.021 --> 13:51.290
attracted to me
or something.

13:51.358 --> 13:53.014
No, I... Oh,
my God, I'm...

13:53.081 --> 13:54.484
I'm so attracted
to you. I...

13:54.552 --> 13:57.193
So why haven't we
done anything about it?

13:57.261 --> 13:59.032
I-I just... you
know, sometimes

13:59.100 --> 14:00.537
taking things
slower is better.

14:00.603 --> 14:02.543
Just ask any sloth.

14:02.611 --> 14:05.854
<i>MALE VOICE: Hey, is sometimes
taking things slower better?</i>

14:11.906 --> 14:13.512
Yeah.

14:13.580 --> 14:17.021
I just... I like
you a lot, and I...

14:17.090 --> 14:18.327
I don't want to
ruin anything

14:18.395 --> 14:19.698
by moving too
fast, you know?

14:19.765 --> 14:21.738
'Cause sometimes,
when you...

14:24.162 --> 14:26.435
Brian, you never told me
you had a beard.

14:26.504 --> 14:27.907
I love beards.

14:27.975 --> 14:29.278
Oh. Yeah.

14:29.346 --> 14:31.485
No, hey, I'm bearding
it up over here.

14:31.553 --> 14:35.347
Hey, Brian, would you be cool
with meeting my parents?

14:35.415 --> 14:36.685
They're in town
this weekend,

14:36.769 --> 14:38.272
and I thought we
could all have dinner.

14:38.341 --> 14:40.046
Uh... sure.

14:40.113 --> 14:42.855
Are they... are they
driving themselves?

14:42.923 --> 14:44.025
(chuckles)

14:44.093 --> 14:46.465
If you're asking
if they can see, yes.

14:46.533 --> 14:49.007
And since you can see...

14:49.075 --> 14:51.716
why don't you tell me
how these look?

14:51.784 --> 14:53.655
Uh... they look
pretty damn great.

14:53.723 --> 14:55.963
Then why don't you
tell me how they feel?

14:56.031 --> 14:57.434
Uh, next time.

14:57.502 --> 14:59.408
Some things are
worth waiting for.

14:59.460 --> 15:01.933
Wow. You're really
a true gentleman.

15:02.000 --> 15:03.504
Yep, not too
many of us left.

15:03.572 --> 15:04.639
(coughing over
shutter clicking)

15:10.425 --> 15:11.345
Stewie,
I need your help.

15:11.413 --> 15:12.365
What? What is it?

15:12.432 --> 15:13.887
I have a crisis situation here.

15:13.955 --> 15:15.474
Kate wants me
to meet her parents.

15:15.542 --> 15:17.331
Hey, guys.

15:17.398 --> 15:20.825
Just gonna...
gonna take this.

15:20.892 --> 15:23.165
Thank you.

15:23.234 --> 15:24.753
What the hell
am I going to do?

15:24.822 --> 15:26.092
All right, all right,
just calm down.

15:26.159 --> 15:27.528
Calm down?

15:27.596 --> 15:29.151
We're all supposed to have
dinner tomorrow night,

15:29.219 --> 15:31.409
and her parents
are going to see that I'm a dog.

15:31.477 --> 15:33.247
(screaming
and groaning)

15:33.316 --> 15:36.557
(repeated bleeping)

15:36.624 --> 15:37.763
Don't worry, Brian.

15:37.829 --> 15:38.999
I'll come up
with something.

15:39.067 --> 15:40.671
Remember, I'm the
guy who came up

15:40.738 --> 15:42.292
<i>with the choreography
to Showgirls.</i>

15:42.343 --> 15:44.532
♪

15:44.601 --> 15:46.524
Okay, stop.
Stop. Stop.

15:46.591 --> 15:49.065
Elizabeth, darling,
too much hands, not enough hips.

15:49.148 --> 15:50.518
Can I just show you?

15:52.058 --> 15:54.082
One, two, three, four.

15:54.148 --> 15:56.270
I'm dancing from my vagina.

15:56.338 --> 15:58.060
One, two, three, four.

15:58.145 --> 16:00.049
I'm grinding, I'm grinding.

16:00.101 --> 16:02.106
Orgasm eyes, orgasm eyes.

16:02.191 --> 16:04.363
And we're done.

16:04.431 --> 16:07.874
You do 20% that,
and we got a movie.

16:12.139 --> 16:14.110
Peter, what
is all this?

16:14.178 --> 16:15.214
Oh, hi, Lois.

16:15.282 --> 16:16.518
I live upstairs now.

16:16.586 --> 16:17.789
What?
That's right.

16:17.857 --> 16:19.628
I made a nest
of my old underwears

16:19.695 --> 16:21.132
on which
to lay my eggs,

16:21.200 --> 16:23.542
and I shall raise my young
in this room alone.

16:23.609 --> 16:24.812
Peter, you're being an idiot.

16:24.878 --> 16:25.948
Oh, really?

16:26.017 --> 16:27.186
Would an idiot
have been able

16:27.271 --> 16:28.875
to rig this rig
to that rig?

16:28.942 --> 16:30.545
Peter, that's nothing.

16:30.613 --> 16:32.502
Oh, is it?

16:36.332 --> 16:38.788
I died! I died!

16:47.868 --> 16:49.892
Oh, hi.
You must be Kate.

16:49.959 --> 16:51.261
I'm Brian's nurse.

16:51.328 --> 16:52.901
He's had a little accident,
I'm afraid.

16:52.969 --> 16:54.941
Oh, my God, Brian!
Are you okay?

16:55.008 --> 16:56.211
Ah, don't worry.
I'm fine.

16:56.278 --> 16:58.001
I'm just sort of
bandaged up right now.

16:58.068 --> 16:59.420
You must be Kate's parents.

16:59.504 --> 17:00.759
It's so nice
to meet you.

17:00.827 --> 17:02.431
Well, it's lovely
to meet you, too.

17:02.499 --> 17:04.102
So what happened?

17:04.170 --> 17:06.694
What happened is this one's
a hero, is what happened.

17:06.763 --> 17:08.934
Rescued two children
from a burning building.

17:09.003 --> 17:10.439
Can you imagine?

17:10.507 --> 17:12.629
Not quite in time-- they
were both horribly burned.

17:12.697 --> 17:14.234
Have that sort of
cr├иme br├╗l├йe face

17:14.303 --> 17:15.990
going on now, but he
saved their lives.

17:16.058 --> 17:17.328
Oh, my, Brian.

17:17.396 --> 17:19.067
I know, right?
So noble.

17:19.135 --> 17:21.040
Plus he's the only
one of my patients

17:21.107 --> 17:23.147
to never ask me
for hand work.

17:23.214 --> 17:24.953
Such a gentleman.

17:25.020 --> 17:26.056
Never even
tried anything

17:26.123 --> 17:27.795
when I'm giving
him a sponge bath.

17:27.862 --> 17:28.964
And I'm very
thorough.

17:29.032 --> 17:30.604
I will wash the
abdominals.

17:30.672 --> 17:32.175
Not all nurses
do, but I do.

17:32.242 --> 17:33.446
And yes, sometimes
I graze it,

17:33.513 --> 17:34.582
but you know what?

17:34.650 --> 17:35.654
I'm a healthcare
professional.

17:35.722 --> 17:37.224
It's what I do.
It's my work.

17:37.292 --> 17:38.362
It's important
to me,

17:38.429 --> 17:40.166
and this one
respects that.

17:40.234 --> 17:43.076
And I'm very
grateful.

17:43.144 --> 17:44.564
Why are you here again?

17:46.321 --> 17:48.109
Oh, my God!
I am so, so sorry.

17:48.178 --> 17:49.880
Uh, it's no problem.
Don't worry about it.

17:49.949 --> 17:50.951
(sniffing)

17:51.020 --> 17:52.389
What's that smell?

17:52.457 --> 17:54.295
It smells like
wet dog in here.

17:55.667 --> 17:58.944
That is the... the
smell of backed up,

17:59.010 --> 18:00.982
unreleased
genital essence.

18:01.051 --> 18:03.658
As I said, he's been
an amazing gentleman.

18:03.726 --> 18:05.714
Well, I'd like
to propose a toast.

18:05.783 --> 18:07.656
To Brian and Kate.

18:07.723 --> 18:09.594
I know we just met,
but you seem

18:09.661 --> 18:11.400
like you're really good
for our daughter.

18:11.468 --> 18:13.038
And risking your
life for those kids?

18:13.106 --> 18:14.342
You're a good
guy, Brian.

18:14.410 --> 18:16.116
A really good guy.

18:16.183 --> 18:17.352
Wow. Thanks.

18:18.873 --> 18:20.195
(rapid thumping)

18:20.263 --> 18:21.867
What's that
thumping noise?

18:21.934 --> 18:23.604
(softly): It's your tail.
Stop wagging your tail.

18:23.672 --> 18:25.245
I can't help it.
Do something.

18:26.398 --> 18:28.405
(groans)

18:28.488 --> 18:30.042
(groaning):
Oh... oh, damn it.

18:30.126 --> 18:31.713
I meant hold it,
not cut it off.

18:31.798 --> 18:32.868
You weren't specific.

18:32.918 --> 18:34.006
I've never done
this before.

18:34.057 --> 18:35.425
Are you okay, Brian?

18:35.509 --> 18:37.884
Yeah, I'm just so happy
to meet you both.

18:39.055 --> 18:40.107
(sizzling)

18:40.192 --> 18:41.695
What the hell
are you...

18:41.746 --> 18:43.869
I'm cauterizing your tail.
Trust me, I'm a nurse.

18:43.937 --> 18:45.040
(stifled groaning)

18:45.108 --> 18:46.176
Brian?

18:46.245 --> 18:47.379
What's going on
over there?

18:47.447 --> 18:49.487
(sniffs) I think
they burned our dinner.

18:49.555 --> 18:51.043
Oh, God, it hurts.
It hurts, Stewie.

18:51.110 --> 18:52.563
Here's a little
morphine.

18:52.614 --> 18:55.005
What the hell? You're not
gonna stick me with that thing.

18:55.073 --> 18:56.776
KATE'S DAD: I don't think
that's a real nurse.

18:56.827 --> 18:58.332
Just hold still.
Pretend you're at the vet.

18:58.416 --> 18:59.620
Vet?
I hate the vet!

18:59.687 --> 19:00.889
(barking angrily)

19:00.958 --> 19:02.579
There's a dog
in here!

19:04.384 --> 19:06.173
Yes! Okay?

19:06.241 --> 19:08.314
There's a dog in here.
I'm a dog!

19:08.316 --> 19:09.484
(gasping)

19:13.631 --> 19:15.369
I'm so sorry, Kate.

19:15.438 --> 19:17.242
I-I know you hate
dogs, and I...

19:17.311 --> 19:19.785
I wanted to tell you--
I-I really did--

19:19.852 --> 19:21.622
but I-I just thought...

19:21.691 --> 19:23.963
I thought, if we got to know
each other better first,

19:24.031 --> 19:25.953
you would eventually
be able to see past it.

19:26.021 --> 19:27.274
STEWIE (chuckles):
"See."

19:27.343 --> 19:29.046
And I... I just... I
really care about you,

19:29.114 --> 19:30.951
and I really want this
to work, and I'm...

19:31.019 --> 19:33.026
I'm so sorry I didn't
tell you before.

19:33.077 --> 19:35.316
Can you ever forgive me?

19:35.384 --> 19:37.556
Do you think that you
can still be with me?

19:37.624 --> 19:39.830
(sighs)
You know what, Brian?

19:39.899 --> 19:42.121
I could have gotten over
the fact that you're a dog,

19:42.188 --> 19:43.843
because I really do
care about you

19:43.911 --> 19:45.582
and I feel like we had
a connection,

19:45.650 --> 19:47.923
but I can't get over the fact
that you lied to me.

19:47.990 --> 19:49.227
You screwed up, Brian.

19:49.296 --> 19:51.065
And now you're
going to have to watch me

19:51.133 --> 19:52.522
walk out that door.

20:00.848 --> 20:03.321
(alarm blaring)

20:03.390 --> 20:04.760
(horn honking, man screaming)

20:04.828 --> 20:05.963
(tires screeching)

20:06.031 --> 20:07.451
(crashing)

20:07.520 --> 20:10.394
Well, it sounds
like I'm needed outside.

20:15.478 --> 20:17.183
Mom, what were
all those carpenters

20:17.250 --> 20:18.386
doing here today?

20:18.454 --> 20:20.191
Putting back our old
crappy stairs, Meg.

20:20.258 --> 20:21.730
I didn't have a choice.

20:21.815 --> 20:23.485
Yay! I love my old stairs!

20:23.554 --> 20:25.526
(giggling)

20:25.593 --> 20:28.116
Uh-oh,
I forgot to cut Joe down.

20:28.202 --> 20:30.693
Joe, what are you
doing up there?

20:30.760 --> 20:32.464
Enjoying Heaven, Bonnie.

20:32.532 --> 20:34.069
Come join me.

20:34.137 --> 20:36.309
There's a gun in
my nightstand.

20:39.069 --> 20:40.338
Brian, I know
you're upset

20:40.407 --> 20:41.743
about what happened with
Kate and everything,

20:41.811 --> 20:43.181
but I did have
one more thought.

20:43.250 --> 20:44.553
Yeah, what's that?

20:44.621 --> 20:45.856
Well, since Kate is blind,

20:45.923 --> 20:47.562
you could probably just
do a different voice

20:47.631 --> 20:49.300
and go out with her
all over again.

20:54.606 --> 20:56.009
BRIAN (nasally):
Hey. Are you Kate?

20:56.034 --> 20:56.811
Yes.

20:56.867 --> 20:59.074
- Hey, it's Noah from JDate.
- Oh, my God! Hi!

20:59.075 --> 22:00.075
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru